WEBVTT

00:00:04.714 --> 00:00:06.215
Hey, Gisey.

00:00:07.341 --> 00:00:10.261
What makes you really happy?

00:00:10.511 --> 00:00:13.264
What brought that on?

00:00:13.514 --> 00:00:15.099
Ready, go!

00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:17.643
"GiSey!
"Coming!

00:00:17.894 --> 00:00:20.521
I'm gonna go help with dinner now!

00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:22.356
'Kay!

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:33.910
<i>Soko ni nani ga aru toshite mo</i>

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:42.585
<i>Mikai no ryouiki e kimi to</i>

00:00:50.843 --> 00:00:58.893
<i>Mijikai yume wo miteta ima</i>

00:00:59.143 --> 00:01:03.522
<i>Are wa kimi no senaka</i>

00:01:03.773 --> 00:01:09.695
<i>Kako? Mirai?</i>

00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:20.456
<i>Furikitte iru meetaa no hari wo mushi shite</i>

00:01:20.706 --> 00:01:23.584
<i>Oikaze to kanjou no muku hou e</i>

00:01:23.834 --> 00:01:29.757
<i>Habataku tabi kizukasareru</i>

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:35.304
<i>Nido to deaenai sora ga aru koto</i>

00:01:35.554 --> 00:01:40.810
<i>Sore demo tobitatsu nara</i>

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:47.608
<i>Kimi no tsubasa ni naru watashi ga</i>

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.378
Northeast wind, wind force 2.

00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:09.171
All clear ahead.

00:02:09.422 --> 00:02:10.631
Helm amidships.

00:02:10.881 --> 00:02:12.508
Helm amidships!

00:02:12.758 --> 00:02:15.344
Looks like we'll have a nice
view of the stars tonight.

00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:25.313
Operation Catch the Silvius Alive!

00:02:28.316 --> 00:02:31.110
Is the table clean, Rene'?

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.903
Yeah.

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:36.282
Help set the table, Fam.

00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:39.577
C'mon, Gisey! Be happier, will you?!

00:02:39.827 --> 00:02:41.370
We're talking about the Silvius!

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:45.708
Can't you just act excited and say,
"Wow, Fam!" or something?

00:02:45.958 --> 00:02:47.501
Oh, the potato pancakes are burning!

00:02:47.752 --> 00:02:50.796
--| love them burned!
--Burned!

00:02:55.051 --> 00:02:57.720
Oh! Would you like some help with that?

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.472
Yes...

00:03:00.806 --> 00:03:03.726
Actually, I think I'll do it myself.

00:03:03.976 --> 00:03:07.688
Why don't any of you seem excited?

00:03:07.938 --> 00:03:11.025
It's the Silvius, you know. The Reaper...

00:03:11.275 --> 00:03:12.276
Reaper?!

00:03:12.526 --> 00:03:15.696
That's right! Silvius, the Reaper!

00:03:15.946 --> 00:03:17.448
Oh!

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.374
Thanks for this...

00:03:26.624 --> 00:03:28.125
It looks really good on you!

00:03:28.376 --> 00:03:30.711
It does?

00:03:30.961 --> 00:03:32.713
Good for you!

00:03:32.963 --> 00:03:34.673
I bet it was real tight here, huh?

00:03:34.924 --> 00:03:37.385
Hey, don't say things like that!

00:03:37.635 --> 00:03:42.765
Hey, you tell them, Millia! Tell 'em,
"We're gonna catch the Silvius!"

00:03:43.015 --> 00:03:45.726
What's the "Silvius"?

00:03:47.269 --> 00:03:50.147
Oh! We caught up to it!

00:03:50.398 --> 00:03:53.609
So that's the Silvius...

00:03:56.487 --> 00:03:58.656
Let's eat!

00:04:04.078 --> 00:04:06.455
Oww, hot!

00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:07.873
I'll serve it to you!

00:04:08.124 --> 00:04:08.958
I love quiche!

00:04:09.208 --> 00:04:11.377
--Oh, me too!
--Nope! None for you!

00:04:11.627 --> 00:04:14.755
--Aww...!
--Stop that. Don't hog it all.

00:04:16.132 --> 00:04:19.635
The Silvius is a mysterious
warship that's really powerful.

00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:24.723
It suddenly showed up in western Lierre
two years ago and then it vanished.

00:04:24.974 --> 00:04:27.309
I've never seen it myself...

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.812
Can you really catch a ghost ship?

00:04:30.062 --> 00:04:31.230
Ghost ship?

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.108
They come for naughty kids!

00:04:34.358 --> 00:04:36.360
Naughty kids?

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:39.947
Don't worry. It's a real ship.

00:04:40.197 --> 00:04:43.951
They say it single-handedly
wiped out an entire Ades fleet.

00:04:44.201 --> 00:04:48.164
So the Federation's desperate to catch it too.

00:04:48.414 --> 00:04:51.459
Sounds too dangerous.
Do we really need such a ship?

00:04:51.709 --> 00:04:56.088
It'll add a lot to your arsenal!
You need one to rebuild Turan, right?

00:04:57.590 --> 00:04:58.924
Good point...

00:04:59.175 --> 00:05:00.176
No, no!

00:05:00.426 --> 00:05:03.095
You're supposed to chomp
into potato pancakes!

00:05:07.183 --> 00:05:09.143
I'm not watching!

00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:12.229
It's okay. You can watch.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.859
When something tastes good,

00:05:17.109 --> 00:05:19.361
you need to make a face...

00:05:19.612 --> 00:05:21.071
...that shows it!

00:05:21.322 --> 00:05:22.907
Oh, right!

00:05:26.827 --> 00:05:30.080
--Is it good?
--Yes, very!

00:05:31.582 --> 00:05:34.168
Okay! Now for everyone's favorite: cured meat!

00:05:34.418 --> 00:05:35.377
Wow!

00:05:35.628 --> 00:05:38.547
It's like a birthday and
harvest festival all at once!

00:05:38.797 --> 00:05:41.217
A birthday! That sounds great!

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.427
Isn't yours coming up, Fam?

00:05:43.677 --> 00:05:46.347
Yeah! I'm about to turn sixteen!

00:05:46.597 --> 00:05:49.141
Hurray! We'll get to eat meat again!

00:05:49.391 --> 00:05:50.309
Meat!

00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:54.522
<i>P</i> It's your birthday! Be happy! <i>P</i>

00:05:54.772 --> 00:05:57.942
P You're born, you live,
and back to dust you go! <i>P</i>

00:05:58.192 --> 00:05:59.985
P-Princess Millia!

00:06:02.112 --> 00:06:04.031
Oh, you...!

00:06:05.783 --> 00:06:09.245
--Your quiche fell apart!
--But it's delicious! --Yum!

00:06:12.331 --> 00:06:13.707
I'm starving...

00:06:13.958 --> 00:06:15.543
Ta-dah!

00:06:15.793 --> 00:06:17.211
This is the Silvius?

00:06:17.461 --> 00:06:18.712
Looks like a fish...

00:06:18.963 --> 00:06:21.757
<i>Where did you get this, Die'?!</i>

00:06:22.007 --> 00:06:23.384
It's a secret!

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:26.345
It's too blurry to make anything out...

00:06:26.595 --> 00:06:30.099
Oh, not necessarily! Right?!

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:33.811
Well, there's reasoning behind
the way ships are built.

00:06:34.061 --> 00:06:38.023
So we can make general deductions
from just tiny bits of information.

00:06:38.274 --> 00:06:39.984
Sounds difficult.

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:44.238
Yes. It's completely different
from any ship we're familiar with.

00:06:44.488 --> 00:06:46.490
I don't know how well it will work...

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.909
What does this look like to you, Gisey?

00:06:49.159 --> 00:06:51.704
Huh? A listening device?

00:06:51.954 --> 00:06:53.956
Then what's this?

00:06:54.206 --> 00:06:56.458
I'd imagine it's a mast...

00:06:56.709 --> 00:06:58.627
Turan ships have them as well.

00:06:58.877 --> 00:07:00.546
Oh, the bridge!

00:07:00.796 --> 00:07:02.548
See? She's got it now!

00:07:03.632 --> 00:07:07.886
Given its comparative size
and structure, it isn't very large...

00:07:08.137 --> 00:07:11.807
It could be a ship-of-the-line--
no, an amphibious assault carrier.

00:07:12.057 --> 00:07:13.475
Amphibious assault carrier?

00:07:13.726 --> 00:07:15.728
Oh, like the one we caught before?

00:07:15.978 --> 00:07:18.272
I don't understand any of this...

00:07:18.522 --> 00:07:19.773
Use your imagination.

00:07:20.024 --> 00:07:21.942
Imagination?

00:07:22.192 --> 00:07:25.738
Now, why is the top flat...?

00:07:25.988 --> 00:07:27.615
Could it be a flight deck?!

00:07:27.865 --> 00:07:29.158
Yeah! Yeah!

00:07:29.408 --> 00:07:30.868
Like a floating dock, then?

00:07:31.118 --> 00:07:33.621
It'd be hard to fight if that were the case.

00:07:33.871 --> 00:07:35.623
A ship-of-the-line, then!

00:07:35.873 --> 00:07:38.083
No, I don't think that's it.

00:07:38.334 --> 00:07:39.501
The Reaper...!

00:07:39.752 --> 00:07:42.004
Rarr!

00:07:42.254 --> 00:07:47.426
Then there's this protrusion
on the bottom... Inside it is...

00:07:47.676 --> 00:07:49.428
I can't really tell...

00:07:49.678 --> 00:07:50.763
<i>I</i> 901: it!

00:07:51.013 --> 00:07:55.976
I bet this pops open and a super secret
weapon starts going, "Kablammo!"

00:07:56.226 --> 00:07:59.730
A secret weapon there!
That would've been neat!

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:01.523
Oh, ballast?

00:08:01.774 --> 00:08:03.108
Yes! Bingo!

00:08:03.359 --> 00:08:04.276
Aww...

00:08:04.526 --> 00:08:07.112
Where's its main armament? Is it unarmed?

00:08:07.363 --> 00:08:09.990
Aww, no secret weapons?

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.117
It's where Fam pointed out earlier.

00:08:12.368 --> 00:08:14.203
You mean they're retractable?!

00:08:14.453 --> 00:08:16.246
Could be where you'd least expect them!

00:08:16.497 --> 00:08:20.125
There aren't any nations with dummy battleships.

00:08:20.376 --> 00:08:24.213
Why would they go so far as to complicate
her structure to hide her weapons?

00:08:24.463 --> 00:08:27.466
Eyewitness reports always
state the ship is alone...

00:08:27.716 --> 00:08:28.926
Oh, I see!

00:08:29.176 --> 00:08:32.262
She must be a solo-operating ship
meant for intelligence gathering!

00:08:32.513 --> 00:08:36.433
So she stays inconspicuous and
avoids fighting whenever possible.

00:08:36.684 --> 00:08:41.355
She's faster than any other ship
and has scouting capabilities

00:08:41.605 --> 00:08:43.857
that allow her to locate
the enemy far in advance.

00:08:44.108 --> 00:08:47.027
Worst of all is that we won't know
what her offensive capabilities are

00:08:47.277 --> 00:08:51.240
until we've landed our first harpoon...

00:08:52.866 --> 00:08:54.785
Done!

00:08:55.035 --> 00:08:56.912
Such a ship really exists...?

00:08:57.162 --> 00:08:58.455
You're amazing, Giselle!

00:08:58.706 --> 00:08:59.581
Huh?

00:08:59.832 --> 00:09:03.669
Yes, this might be my best work yet!

00:09:03.919 --> 00:09:07.256
--All finished! Now this is Silvius...
--...the Reaper!

00:09:07.506 --> 00:09:08.757
Wow!

00:09:09.007 --> 00:09:11.427
It's got secret weapons up the wazoo!

00:09:14.012 --> 00:09:18.308
All it needs now... is a little water!

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:20.561
Don't sleep!

00:09:20.811 --> 00:09:23.063
Don't sleep, Fritz!

00:09:40.748 --> 00:09:42.958
That really is how it is, though...

00:09:45.669 --> 00:09:47.838
Oh, a shooting star!

00:09:48.088 --> 00:09:49.965
He's certainly an unusual character.

00:09:50.215 --> 00:09:51.175
Yeah.

00:09:51.425 --> 00:09:56.263
He suddenly showed up about half a year
ago and wound up staying with us.

00:09:56.513 --> 00:10:01.477
He's got skill, all right,
but he's also kinda flaky...

00:10:04.772 --> 00:10:06.899
Are you hungry, Millia?

00:10:07.149 --> 00:10:09.193
--I'm fine.
--Really?

00:10:14.406 --> 00:10:16.325
Mmm! Smells nice!

00:10:16.575 --> 00:10:20.120
Aunt Tereza sure knows how to dry 'em good!

00:10:28.921 --> 00:10:30.672
Want some water, Millia?

00:10:30.923 --> 00:10:32.591
Oh, don't make a fuss on account of me.

00:10:32.841 --> 00:10:36.261
Don't be shy. Think of it as your own home.

00:10:36.512 --> 00:10:39.973
Although it is pretty small...

00:10:44.228 --> 00:10:45.938
It's been a while since I've had a guest!

00:10:46.188 --> 00:10:48.106
What about Giselle?

00:10:48.357 --> 00:10:51.109
Just once, a long time ago.

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:54.613
She has to look after René
and the others, after all.

00:10:57.282 --> 00:11:00.118
It's all yours, Princess!

00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:02.079
What about you?

00:11:04.581 --> 00:11:05.749
The floor?

00:11:05.999 --> 00:11:07.751
You take the bed!

00:11:08.001 --> 00:11:09.920
You're the guest, you know.

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.422
--Give me that!
--No!

00:11:12.673 --> 00:11:14.716
--Why not?
--You have the bed.

00:11:14.967 --> 00:11:17.177
I'll sleep on the floor!

00:11:17.427 --> 00:11:19.471
I'm not sure a princess can handle it...

00:11:19.721 --> 00:11:21.431
Come again?!

00:11:28.397 --> 00:11:32.651
Why did you make such a crazy announcement

00:11:32.901 --> 00:11:35.445
and drag the people of Kartoffel into this?

00:11:35.696 --> 00:11:39.241
It's not like we need the Silvius...

00:11:39.491 --> 00:11:42.786
The bigger the prey, the better, I figure!

00:11:43.036 --> 00:11:45.122
Wouldn't that make you happier?

00:11:49.793 --> 00:11:52.462
I just want to make you happy, is all...

00:11:56.341 --> 00:11:58.552
It doesn't make you happy?

00:12:00.762 --> 00:12:03.015
--You're so dumb.
--Huh?!

00:12:03.265 --> 00:12:05.767
Hey now, Millia...

00:12:09.897 --> 00:12:12.232
Goodnight, Fam.

00:12:14.735 --> 00:12:17.029
Goodnight, Millia!

00:12:31.752 --> 00:12:35.088
First harpoon... Boom!

00:12:35.339 --> 00:12:36.715
Johann's Vanship?!

00:12:36.965 --> 00:12:38.008
Fan'!

00:12:38.258 --> 00:12:39.760
Yeah, I heard!

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:42.971
Let's go catch the Reaper!

00:12:46.808 --> 00:12:49.853
<i>I will</i> rebuild Turan.

00:12:50.103 --> 00:12:54.942
Please watch over me, Father... Sister...

00:13:07.746 --> 00:13:10.415
Come back safely!

00:13:10.666 --> 00:13:13.251
--We're going too!
--Y-You can't be serious!

00:13:13.502 --> 00:13:16.004
- Teddy!
--You shouldn't, Princess.

00:13:16.254 --> 00:13:17.798
I want to go.

00:13:19.424 --> 00:13:22.094
All right. Be careful!

00:13:22.344 --> 00:13:24.388
--| will!
--Wha...?!

00:13:28.725 --> 00:13:30.852
Let's have some fun...

00:13:31.103 --> 00:13:34.940
Millia! Wow! Nice outfit!

00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:36.900
Let's go!

00:13:40.862 --> 00:13:42.322
Maybe this isn't such a good idea...

00:13:42.572 --> 00:13:46.076
What's the matter? You were brimming
with confidence just last night...

00:13:46.326 --> 00:13:47.661
It's just...

00:13:47.911 --> 00:13:52.833
Don't worry. I believe in you.
If anyone can pull this off, it's us!

00:13:53.083 --> 00:13:54.918
Fam...

00:13:55.168 --> 00:13:56.628
Yeah.

00:13:57.963 --> 00:14:00.757
This one's different from Pam's...

00:14:01.008 --> 00:14:02.509
Hands off!

00:14:05.721 --> 00:14:07.472
Sorry.

00:14:07.723 --> 00:14:10.767
That's Lucciola's seat...

00:14:13.562 --> 00:14:16.023
You might want to keep your mouth closed!

00:14:17.649 --> 00:14:19.067
Corkscrew!

00:14:19.317 --> 00:14:22.154
S-Stop! D-Don't...!

00:14:27.409 --> 00:14:30.454
That hits the spot!

00:14:30.704 --> 00:14:32.414
Did you sleep good, Fam?

00:14:32.664 --> 00:14:34.750
--Yep!
--Well enough to fall.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:36.543
Eight times now!

00:14:37.919 --> 00:14:39.838
--How's the Skyfish?
--Just woke up.

00:14:40.088 --> 00:14:42.591
She's taking it nice and easy.

00:14:42.841 --> 00:14:43.717
Right around here.

00:14:43.967 --> 00:14:46.470
All right! We'll go with our usual plan!

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:48.305
We're facing the Reaper, you know...

00:14:48.555 --> 00:14:51.558
That's why we gotta play it by the book;
we don't know anything about her!

00:14:55.937 --> 00:14:58.190
We're here!

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:00.025
Millia! And Teddy!

00:15:00.275 --> 00:15:01.902
Oh, my...

00:15:02.152 --> 00:15:05.238
D-Don't bother telling me to leave! I refuse to!

00:15:05.489 --> 00:15:07.324
You can't leave, you mean.

00:15:07.574 --> 00:15:12.245
Sure, you can watch. We <i>will</i>
catch the Silvius for you!

00:15:13.997 --> 00:15:16.541
Seven ships dead-ahead! Distance, 30,000!

00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:21.004
Signal flares detected!
Identifies as Federation ship Qingu!

00:15:21.254 --> 00:15:22.923
10 to port.

00:15:23.173 --> 00:15:24.674
10 to port!

00:15:28.678 --> 00:15:30.263
Skyfish has altered course!

00:15:30.514 --> 00:15:32.682
Ha! Ostrich-brain!

00:15:42.818 --> 00:15:44.736
Okay! First harpoon!

00:15:44.986 --> 00:15:45.737
Cecily.

00:15:45.987 --> 00:15:48.490
They said, "First harpoon!"

00:15:56.790 --> 00:15:58.333
Speed is dropping!

00:15:58.583 --> 00:15:59.584
Captain.

00:15:59.835 --> 00:16:02.212
So this is a Skyfish hunt?

00:16:03.964 --> 00:16:06.216
You seem to be enjoying yourself.

00:16:06.466 --> 00:16:08.552
All right! We stopped her!

00:16:09.928 --> 00:16:11.012
It's still roaring...?

00:16:11.263 --> 00:16:14.599
Leave it to me! I'll blind the Reaper!

00:16:19.104 --> 00:16:22.190
--Is this what I think it is?
--Blinders?

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.902
Multiple rocks ahead. Distance, 500.

00:16:26.153 --> 00:16:27.654
20 to starboard!

00:16:28.697 --> 00:16:30.490
Climb to 75!

00:16:33.869 --> 00:16:35.954
She has really good ears!

00:16:36.204 --> 00:16:37.998
Then let's plug 'em!

00:16:46.756 --> 00:16:48.717
M)' apologies...

00:16:48.967 --> 00:16:52.012
--It's all right.
--Alis. You handle it from here.

00:17:06.026 --> 00:17:10.614
"You're now blind and deaf.
Your ship doesn't stand a chance now.

00:17:10.864 --> 00:17:14.034
If you surrender, Fam Fan Fan of Kartoffel

00:17:14.284 --> 00:17:16.786
will lead you to a safe location."

00:17:18.455 --> 00:17:20.624
I hope this'll get Millia excited!

00:17:21.917 --> 00:17:23.960
Playing war, are you?

00:17:27.464 --> 00:17:28.215
The enemy?!

00:17:28.465 --> 00:17:30.550
The Silvius is getting away!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:34.221
Roger! We'll knock out
its listening device again!

00:17:38.350 --> 00:17:40.518
--Fam!
--We can't shake her!

00:17:44.105 --> 00:17:46.524
--A passing mark, but just barely.
--Who do you think you are?!

00:17:46.775 --> 00:17:48.985
Your Scissors needs work.

00:17:50.737 --> 00:17:53.031
--Go help them!
--What for?

00:17:53.281 --> 00:17:56.034
See? She's having so much fun!

00:17:56.284 --> 00:17:58.662
“Hang On tight!
“Right!

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:10.757
Going to ram me, huh?

00:18:11.007 --> 00:18:12.509
Now!

00:18:16.638 --> 00:18:20.684
She didn't shoot at us. What do we do now?!

00:18:20.934 --> 00:18:23.520
Unarmed, huh? Sounds interesting.

00:18:28.566 --> 00:18:30.902
Let me join in too!

00:18:37.742 --> 00:18:40.328
Huh? Why...?

00:18:43.456 --> 00:18:46.918
--Are we alive...?
--Yeah, somehow.

00:18:47.168 --> 00:18:49.587
Where's the Skyfish, Gisey?

00:18:51.715 --> 00:18:53.008
There! Four o'clock!

00:18:53.258 --> 00:18:55.176
Distance, 4,000!

00:18:55.427 --> 00:18:56.928
The Grand Lake!

00:19:03.393 --> 00:19:04.769
That's sacred land...!

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:07.564
Stop! Let's forget about catching it!

00:19:07.814 --> 00:19:09.983
We're doing this for you, you know...

00:19:10.233 --> 00:19:11.735
But...!

00:19:11.985 --> 00:19:13.486
<i>Pam'?!</i>

00:19:17.073 --> 00:19:20.243
Don't worry! We won't
desecrate the Grand Lake!

00:19:20.493 --> 00:19:21.244
<i>Pam'?!</i>

00:19:21.494 --> 00:19:23.204
Shoot it, Gisey!

00:19:27.834 --> 00:19:30.378
--Try again, Gisey!
--It's no use.

00:19:30.628 --> 00:19:35.258
I've never successfully stopped a
Claudia engine, not even during training...

00:19:35.508 --> 00:19:38.219
How about from the inside, then?!

00:19:38.470 --> 00:19:41.056
It's okay. I know you can do it!

00:19:42.349 --> 00:19:45.435
Okay. I'll give it a shot!

00:19:49.064 --> 00:19:50.857
Straight for six seconds, then go up.

00:19:51.107 --> 00:19:54.027
Four, three, two, one...

00:19:54.277 --> 00:19:55.779
Now!

00:19:56.654 --> 00:20:01.076
Who knows? Ships like this might be
surprisingly spacious down below!

00:20:01.326 --> 00:20:04.454
Make a right in three, two, one...

00:20:04.704 --> 00:20:06.039
Now!

00:20:06.289 --> 00:20:08.333
Wow! You're amazing, Gisey!

00:20:08.583 --> 00:20:11.920
All it needs now is a little water!

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:14.839
Water...? Watertight doors?!

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.884
--No! Take us out, Fam!
--Huh?!

00:20:20.095 --> 00:20:22.764
Outer watertight doors sealed.

00:20:23.014 --> 00:20:25.850
Tween deck evacuation complete.

00:20:26.101 --> 00:20:28.645
All hands, brace yourselves!

00:20:28.895 --> 00:20:31.064
--Go back!
--Yeah!

00:20:33.483 --> 00:20:34.984
Fan'!

00:20:40.990 --> 00:20:43.576
Oh, no! Why is it...?!

00:20:54.421 --> 00:20:56.214
Gisey...

00:20:56.464 --> 00:20:59.426
I dreamed the Skyfish dove underwater...

00:21:02.762 --> 00:21:05.098
It wasn't a dream.

00:21:05.348 --> 00:21:08.685
We can go anywhere in
the sky and sea we want.

00:21:08.935 --> 00:21:10.228
Doesn't that sound wonderful?

00:21:10.478 --> 00:21:14.274
Now that you've seen the Silvius,
we can't let you leave alive.

00:21:14.524 --> 00:21:17.360
You were in that red Vanship.

00:21:17.610 --> 00:21:20.530
I am Captain Tatiana Wisla.

00:21:21.656 --> 00:21:24.325
Fam Fan Fan of Kartoffel.

00:21:24.576 --> 00:21:26.161
How old are you?

00:21:30.874 --> 00:21:34.752
I'm Giselle Collette. W-We're both fifteen.

00:21:35.003 --> 00:21:39.466
We could return you to the sky,
if you'll agree to help us.

00:21:39.716 --> 00:21:41.593
What do you want out of us?

00:21:44.971 --> 00:21:46.514
Hmm...

00:21:46.764 --> 00:21:50.935
Go steal some Ades Federation ships--
one for each year you've been alive.

00:21:51.186 --> 00:21:52.312
One for each year?!

00:21:52.562 --> 00:21:55.231
We can't steal fifteen ships!

00:21:55.482 --> 00:21:57.692
Too much for you kids to handle?

00:21:58.943 --> 00:22:02.238
All right, then! We'll swipe fifteen for you!

00:22:06.034 --> 00:22:07.577
Fam! Giselle!

00:22:07.827 --> 00:22:09.370
Millia...

00:22:14.834 --> 00:22:16.544
Deal.

00:22:16.794 --> 00:22:19.547
We'll put an entire fleet together
if we have to, for Millia!

00:22:19.797 --> 00:22:21.424
Huh?!

00:22:30.892 --> 00:22:36.481
<i>Sora wa dore hodo takai no darou</i>

00:22:36.731 --> 00:22:42.529
<i>Kaze wa dore hodo tsuyoi no darou</i>

00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:48.368
<i>Mizu wa dore hodo sunderu darou</i>

00:22:48.618 --> 00:22:55.667
<i>Kimi no mune no naka dewa</i>

00:22:56.876 --> 00:23:08.346
<i>Namida uketomeru
kimi no te no hira ni itsuka naritai</i>

00:23:08.596 --> 00:23:20.441
<i>Onaji kanashimi onaji kuuki wo wakeaitai</i>

00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:26.281
<i>lma hashiridasu fune no saki wo</i>

00:23:26.531 --> 00:23:35.081
<i>Tamerawazu kimi no muki e susumete</i>

00:23:35.331 --> 00:23:41.045
<i>Kaze no umi de hobashira wo tate</i>

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:46.843
<i>Kumo no nami wo suberihajimeyou</i>

00:23:47.093 --> 00:23:52.599
<i>Tooi hoshi wo konpasu ni shite</i>

00:23:52.849 --> 00:24:00.523
<i>Kimi to mezasu kanata e</i>

00:24:02.483 --> 00:24:05.153
<i>Urgh! What's with that woman captain?!</i>

00:24:05.403 --> 00:24:07.864
<i>Thinks she's hot stuff just 'cause
she's decent with a Vanship!</i>

00:24:08.114 --> 00:24:09.324
<i>I'm gonna show her a thing or two!</i>

00:24:09.574 --> 00:24:12.869
<i>But it's like we've fallen right into their laps.</i>

00:24:13.119 --> 00:24:17.290
<i>Do you think Dio planned for the Silvius
to catch us from the very start?!</i>

00:24:17.540 --> 00:24:22.920
<i>--Huh?! You're suggesting he's a Silvius spy?
-- P It's your birthday! Be happy! P</i>

00:24:23.171 --> 00:24:25.673
<i>P You're born, you live,
and back to dust you go! P</i>

00:24:25.923 --> 00:24:28.176
<i>--He's definitely not.
--Agreed.</i>

00:24:28.426 --> 00:24:30.720
<i>lmmelmann Turn!</i>
